        "title": "Find least common denominator",
        "text": "Write in terms of a common denominator $$x\\left(x+1\\right)$$",
        "variabilization": {},
        "oer": "",
        "license": ""
    },
    {
        "id": "ace4be0A1-diag-P15a-h2",
        "type": "hint",
        "dependencies": [
            "ace4be0A1-diag-P15a-h1"
        ],
        "title": "Common Denominator",
        "text": "$$\\frac{3}{x\\left(x+1\\right)}+\\frac{\\frac{1}{x} \\left(x+1\\right)}{x+1}=\\frac{1}{x+1} \\frac{x}{x}+\\frac{2\\left(x\\left(x+1\\right)\\right)}{x\\left(x+1\\right)}$$",
        "variabilization": {},
        "oer": "",
        "license": ""
    },
    {
        "id": "ace4be0A1-diag-P15a-h3",
        "type": "hint",
        "dependencies": [
            "ace4be0A1-diag-P15a-h2"
        ],
        "title": "Combing common terms",
        "text": "$$\\frac{3+x+1}{x\\left(x+1\\right)}=\\frac{x+2x^2+2x}{x\\left(x+1\\right)}$$",
        "variabilization": {},
        "oer": "",
        "license": ""
    },
    {
        "id": "ace4be0A1-diag-P15a-h4",
        "type": "hint",
        "dependencies": [
            "ace4be0A1-diag-P15a-h3"
        ],
        "title": "Move all terms to RHS",
        "text": "$$0=\\frac{2x^2+3x-x-4}{x\\left(x+1\\right)}=\\frac{2x^2+2x-4}{x\\left(x+1\\right)}$$",
        "variabilization": {},
        "oer": "",
        "license": ""
    },
    {
        "id": "ace4be0A1-diag-P15a-h5",
        "type": "hint",
        "dependencies": [
            "ace4be0A1-diag-P15a-h4"
        ],
        "title": "Factor numerator",
        "text": "$$2x^2+2x-4=2\\left(x^2+x-2\\right)=2\\left(x+2\\right) \\left(x-1\\right)$$",
        "variabilization": {},
        "oer": "",
        "license": ""
    },
    {
        "id": "ace4be0A1-diag-P15a-h6",
        "type": "hint",
        "dependencies": [
            "ace4be0A1-diag-P15a-h5"
        ],
        "title": "Interpret",
        "text": "We cannot have the denominator be zero, which means that $$x$$ cannot be $$0$$ or $$-1$$. But the numerator must be zero, which only happens if $$x-1=0$$ or $$x+2=0$$.",
        "variabilization": {},
        "oer": "",
        "license": ""
    }
